engine: controls for a GoldSrc demo — pause, speed, seek, and its state

demo_pause holds the demo; demo_speed (0.25 to 4) scales the whole host
frame while one plays, so the game's clock, the animations and the
recording agree; demo_seek <seconds> runs the frames in between without
waiting (a few hundred per host frame, so the page keeps breathing, and the
client-side sounds and events on the way are not replayed) — backward by
starting the demo again and carrying the target across. The reader keeps
its own section clock instead of Xash's start-time arithmetic, and the
angle interpolation reads that clock. Demo_WebState(), exported to the
page, says where the demo is: time, length, paused, seeking, speed,
section, protocol, whether the recording is a spectator's, the map.

